<title>USA: Mine Safety names Thomas Hotopp president.</title>
<headline>Mine Safety names Thomas Hotopp president.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mine Safety Appliances said it named Thomas Hotopp president of the company to replace John Ryan, the company's chairman and chief executive who formerly held the title of president as well.</p>
<p>The company did not say when the move was effective. It was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Hotopp joined the company in 1991 after serving as president of the Kingston-Warren Corp of Newfields, N.H.</p>
<p>As president, Hotopp will oversee all of the company's U.S. operations.</p>
</text>
